    "what_is_it": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_1": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Does Hair Go Grey?",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Hair colour comes from melanin, produced by cells in each hair follicle. As we age — or due to genetics, stress, and other factors — those cells gradually slow down or stop producing pigment, and new hair grows in grey or white. It's a normal, natural process, and it happens at a different pace for everyone.</p><ul><li><strong>Genetics</strong> — the biggest factor in when and how fast grey appears</li><li><strong>Age</strong> — pigment-producing cells naturally slow down over time</li><li><strong>Stress &amp; lifestyle</strong> — can accelerate the process in some people</li></ul><p>It's also something you're allowed to have an opinion about — including choosing to cover it, on your own terms, without turning it into a whole event.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["heading_1", "text_1"],
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-7",
        "full_width": true,
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48
      }
    },
    "frustrations": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_1": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The Part Nobody Talks About",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A few of the most common frustrations people share about covering grey hair:</p><ul><li>Spotting the first few strands, then checking the mirror a little more often after that</li><li>Booking, paying for, and scheduling around salon appointments every few weeks</li><li>Mixing, timing, and cleaning up traditional dye — turning colour into a whole event</li><li>Positioning yourself so the grey around your hairline isn't the first thing people notice in photos</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["heading_1", "text_1"],
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-6",
        "full_width": true,
        "padding_top": 48,
