    "how_it_helps": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_1": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A Simpler Way to Cover Grey",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Corvina is a wash-in herbal formula built around Polygonum multiflorum (he shou wu), a botanical long used in traditional hair care. Rich pigments coat each strand as you wash, gradually building colour with repeated use — no ammonia, no mixing, no timer.</p><p>It won't replace a full salon transformation overnight, and we won't pretend otherwise — but it's a real, honest way to keep grey covered as part of your normal routine.</p>",
            "text_style": "subtitle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["heading_1", "text_1"],
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-7",
        "full_width": true,
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48
      }
    },
    "how_to_use": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_1": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How to Use It",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>1. Apply</strong> — work into wet hair like a normal shampoo, focusing on roots and grey areas.</p><p><strong>2. Lather &amp; wait</strong> — massage through, leave for a few minutes so the pigment can coat each strand.</p><p><strong>3. Rinse &amp; repeat</strong> — rinse thoroughly. Colour builds gradually, so repeat with each wash until you reach your shade, then use as needed to maintain it.</p>"
          }
        },
